        <mxCell id="fn" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontColor=#5A6C7D;" value="&lt;b&gt;Subnet CIDRs are deliberately not shown.&lt;/b&gt; eks-cluster.yaml sets no &lt;code&gt;vpc.cidr&lt;/code&gt;, so eksctl assigns them &amp;#8212; printing invented ranges would be the one thing on this page a reviewer could check and find wrong. Read them from the live VPC.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Nothing on this page crosses a boundary it does not really cross.&lt;/b&gt; Instances sit in subnets; the node group, the ALB and the Gateway Endpoint are objects above the subnet level, so each is drawn once at its own scope rather than duplicated per AZ." vertex="1">
